Diagnostic: log the ScrollingEffectsController identity on the kinetic wheel path.

The phase-split fix (webkit-wheel-coalesce-phase-split.patch) removed the giant
coalesced merges but franceinfo still stops dead, and the historySize counter now
shows why it is a different bug: on flick N the first motion event already sees a
non-zero historySize (stale entries from flick N-1 that were never consumed), while
the Ended event that arms the fling sees historySize=0. That is only possible if the
motion events and the gesture-end event reach DIFFERENT ScrollingEffectsController
instances - motion builds node A's history, the Ended event arms node B whose history
is empty, so the fling computes from one sample. Log `this` on both trace lines to
confirm the split directly rather than infer it. Diagnostic only.

Must apply AFTER webkit-kinetic-wheel-path-diagnostic.patch (edits its log lines).

